<header><p class="st-kicker">crusader state · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Principality of Antioch</h1><p class="st-meta">1098 CE – 1268 CE · capital Antioch</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Norman-founded Crusader principality in northern Syria that lasted 170 years until Baybars destroyed its capital in 1268.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-crusade">First Crusade</a> besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a> from October 1097 and took it in June 1098, then defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kerbogha">Kerbogha's</a> relief army. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemond-i-of-antioch">Bohemond of Taranto</a>, a Norman from southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, kept the city for himself despite promises to return it to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/byzantium">Byzantium</a>, founding the principality.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch's</a> princes ruled a population of Greek <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenians">Armenians</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syriac-christians">Syriac Christians</a> and Muslims, with Italian merchants in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latakia">Latakia</a> and the port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/port-of-saint-symeon">Saint Symeon</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assizes-of-antioch">Assizes of Antioch</a> codified its law. Its army was crushed at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ager-sanguinis">Field of Blood</a> in 1119, and in 1137 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raymond-of-poitiers">Raymond of Poitiers</a> had to accept Byzantine overlordship. In the 13th century it was united with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-tripoli">County of Tripoli</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemond-vi-of-antioch">Bohemond VI</a> submitted to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> in 1260.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a> sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baybars">Baybars</a> stormed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a> in May 1268, killing or enslaving much of its population; the city never regained its former importance. The title Prince of Antioch survived in the house of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-tripoli">Tripoli</a> and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/principality-of-antioch.jpg" alt="Principality of Antioch" width="320" height="208"><figcaption>Image: Dragovit · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Banner_of_the_Principality_of_Antioch.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1098 CE – 1268 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>crusader state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Antioch</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Bohemond I, Raymond of Poitiers, Bohemond VI</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Latin Christianity, Eastern Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old French, Greek, Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a>, <a href="/countries/syria">Syria</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Antioch</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1183&amp;focus=principality-of-antioch" aria-label="Principality of Antioch on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5591 871 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Principality of Antioch lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5911 1127L5709 970M5911 1127L5911 1187M5911 1127L5815 1335M5911 1127L5890 1101"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5709 970h0M5911 1187h0M5815 1335h0M5890 1101h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5911 1127h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5911 1127h0"/></svg></a><figcapti